<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ApprovalProcess xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ApprovalProcess> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error. The rationale below lives in this comment
        rather than in <description> because a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the
        Metadata API. ⚠ DO NOT ASSUME THE 255-CHARACTER CAP that binds RecordType and
        ValidationRule descriptions applies here: the five approval files already in this repo
        carry descriptions of 442 to 617 characters (measured against git HEAD, 2026-08-19).
        The descriptions written in this change are nevertheless kept under 255, so the rule is
        uniform across every metadata type in this tranche and never has to be re-measured.

        NEW 2026-08-19. Disposition_Offer__c had no approval process before this change.

        IT APPROVES THE OFFER, NOT THE DISPOSITION, for the same reason Broker_Finalize_Approval
        approves the submission: the approval page then shows the terms actually being decided -
        price, earnest money, due-diligence and closing periods, financing type - rather than a
        Disposition that carries none of them.

        🔴 THIS IS THE SECOND HALF OF A TWO-STEP TRANSITION (design D-3), AND THE ORDER IS THE
        POINT. Selecting an offer ALREADY moved the Disposition from Active Listing (on-market)
        or Release Materials (off-market) to Offer Selection, by explicit service DML inside
        DispositionApprovalService.selectOffer, under a savepoint, in the same transaction that
        submitted this approval. So:
          - APPROVED  -> DispositionOfferTriggerHandler sets this offer's Offer_Status__c to
                         'Accepted', moves the parent from Offer Selection to LOI (only if the
                         parent is CURRENTLY on Offer Selection) and stamps
                         Accepted_Offer_Price__c. The LOI stage entry then auto-creates the
                         sell-side LOI through the existing DispositionStageEntryService.
          - REJECTED  -> nothing moves. The deal is PARKED at Offer Selection for a re-pick.
        The alternative - advancing only on approval - would leave a submitted deal sitting at
        Active Listing as though no offer had been chosen. The stage always tells the truth.

        ENTRY IS Is_Selected__c = true, which is written exclusively (at most one selected offer
        per disposition) by selectOffer. The parent's stage is deliberately NOT in the entry
        criteria: selectOffer asserts it before it writes anything, and duplicating the assert
        here would make a cross-object criterion out of a check the service already performs.

        🔴 recordEditability = AdminOnly LOCKS THIS OFFER, NOT THE PARENT DISPOSITION. That is
        precisely why DispositionOfferTriggerHandler may update the parent SYNCHRONOUSLY with
        allOrNone = false in SYSTEM mode, and why no semaphore or Queueable is needed here. The
        three Disposition-target approvals lock the very record they must advance, which is why
        THEY need the D-1 route.
        ⚠ THE COROLLARY: while this approval is pending the offer's own fields are locked. Any
        counter-negotiation must therefore be recalled first, which is why allowRecall stays true.

        ⚠ Approval_Status__c IS A SECOND, DISTINCT PICKLIST FROM Offer_Status__c on this object.
        The trigger WRITES the second from the first; they are not interchangeable. It requires
        BOTH Approved AND Is_Selected__c, plus the parent's current-stage guard.

        approvalPageFields carry only fields DPEG_Disposition_View already grants read on - an
        approver who cannot read a field on the approval page sees a blank, not an error.
        Is_Selected__c is included and gains read FLS in the same deploy.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. workflows/Disposition_Offer__c.workflow-meta.xml and both
        of objects/Disposition_Offer__c/fields/{Approval_Status__c, Is_Selected__c} must land
        FIRST.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <allowRecall>true</allowRecall>
    <allowedSubmitters>
        <type>owner</type>
    </allowedSubmitters>
    <approvalPageFields>
        <field>Name</field>
        <field>Owner</field>
        <field>Buyer_Name__c</field>
        <field>Offer_Amount__c</field>
        <field>Offer_Date__c</field>
        <field>Earnest_Money_Proposed__c</field>
        <field>Due_Diligence_Days__c</field>
        <field>Closing_Period_Days__c</field>
        <field>Offer_Financing_Type__c</field>
        <field>Is_Selected__c</field>
    </approvalPageFields>
    <approvalStep>
        <allowDelegate>false</allowDelegate>
        <assignedApprover>
            <approver>
                <name>nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <approver>
                <name>aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@avanzasolutions.com</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <whenMultipleApprovers>FirstResponse</whenMultipleApprovers>
        </assignedApprover>
        <label>Principal Review</label>
        <name>Principal_Review_Step</name>
    </approvalStep>
    <description>Principal sign-off on the offer chosen for this disposition. Entry: Is Selected is true. Approval sets Approval Status, which accepts the offer and advances the parent Disposition from Offer Selection to LOI. Rejection parks the deal at Offer Selection.</description>
    <enableMobileDeviceAccess>false</enableMobileDeviceAccess>
    <entryCriteria>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Disposition_Offer__c.Is_Selected__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>True</value>
        </criteriaItems>
    </entryCriteria>
    <finalApprovalActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Offer_Approval_Approved</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalApprovalActions>
    <finalApprovalRecordLock>false</finalApprovalRecordLock>
    <finalRejectionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Offer_Approval_Rejected</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalRejectionActions>
    <finalRejectionRecordLock>false</finalRejectionRecordLock>
    <label>Offer Selection Approval</label>
    <processOrder>1</processOrder>
    <recordEditability>AdminOnly</recordEditability>
    <showApprovalHistory>true</showApprovalHistory>
</ApprovalProcess>
